        "title": "The Metaphor Outruns the Product",
        "description": "Calling Twilite 'the matrix' could promise immersion, intelligence, and coherence before the everyday browser experience earns those expectations.",
        "likelihood": "medium",
        "impact": "high",
        "mitigation": "Use the metaphor as a product test: every claimed matrix capability must correspond to an observable browsing advantage and a stable graph contract.",
        "definitionKey": "idea-risk",
